.SS IS__REGPARM__SUPPORTED
.IP
.EX
#define IS__REGPARM__SUPPORTED
.EE
.PP
Checks whether the \f[CR]REGPARM\f[R] macro is defined as non\-empty.
This indicates that the compiler truly supports the \f[CR]regparm\f[R]
attribute.
.RS
.PP
Note:
.PP
Checking \f[CR]IS__REGPARM__SUPPORTED\f[R] alone is not sufficient.
.PP
You must also verify that your target architecture and compiler supports
regparm.
.RE
.PP
Example:
.IP
.EX
#ifdef IS__REGPARM__SUPPORTED
int REGPARM(3) fast_add(int a, int b, int c);
#else
int fast_add(int a, int b, int c);
#endif
.EE
